		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=15949&amp;sid=2ad893443a04e6cf26d76733e357770d#15949"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Thu Sep 26, 2002 8:31 am<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=15949&amp;sid=2ad893443a04e6cf26d76733e357770d"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Arialana walks quietly into the guildhall, watching as Lanturias is taught by his guildmaster. She sits down on the hall steps awaiting her moment to speak.  When the guild master has become quiet, Arialana clears her throat softly hoping to gather Lanturias' attention without startling him.  Lanturias opens his eyes and turns around to see Arialana sitting on the steps. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;Pardon my interruption, but I must speak with Lanturias. Follow me Lanturias.&quot;  She waves for him to come over to her and then starts walking outside the guild hall.  She turns to make sure Lanturias has followed behind her, in seeing that he did she then speaks. &quot;Lanturias, I do not think I need to tell you why I came to find you.  That event in the Kindred Spirits is quite obviously the reason.  You are a mild mannered man, I have never known you to harm anything that is not an evil being that deserves the harm.  Now with that being said, What is your explanation for what you did to Jesent?  Jesent is both our friends and you have to know whatever he does is out of friendship and certainly does not warrant that type of rebuttal.  Well, so what is going on with you? You know you can talk to me about it.&quot; Arialana gazes at Lanturias awaiting his response. 
<br />
<i></i><br />_________________<br />Arialana Nightingale
<br />
Healer of the sick, Rezzer of the dead for 50 seasons
<br />
<img src="images/smiles/new_angel.gif" alt="new_angel.gif" border="0" />
<br />
Llaianya Natursangel
<br />
Preserver of the Wild for 59 seasons</span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
