		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=15951&amp;sid=2ad893443a04e6cf26d76733e357770d#15951"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Mon Sep 30, 2002 5:16 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=15951&amp;sid=2ad893443a04e6cf26d76733e357770d"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">&quot;You are right Lanturias. Keeping it bottled up inside of you is not very healthy at all. If you would like some tips on anger management, here is the best I have found. If you should find yourself in a foul mood and angry, go find the nearest foul creature and give it a good whack or two. That seems to reduce the anger a good extent, at least for me. Try it next time, and notice I said foul creature.  Friends do not count as foul, at least not real ones.&quot; Arialana chuckles. &quot;No plans at the moment, I will come with to the Kindred spirits. It is due time you apologized to Jesent, as well as afterwards revealing to me what your problem is.  I am here to help you as your friend, but we will deal with that in a bit. Let's off and go.&quot; Arialana puts her arm over Lanturias' shoulder moving him forward slightly. 
<br />
<i></i><br />_________________<br />Arialana Nightingale
<br />
